WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.080
- Millie, we just re-hydrated the brisket.

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:02.980
- Mm-hm.

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.570
- We left it on for
about 10 or 15 minutes,

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:07.380
which kind of surprised me, but it's like,

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:08.600
that's what's gonna do it.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:11.160
Give it the time, invest in it.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.960
And now what are we doing?

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:16.370
- So we're gonna take our
leftover macaroni and cheese.

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:17.290
I mean, oftentimes,

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:19.401
there's never any leftover
macaroni and cheese.

00:00:19.401 --> 00:00:20.811
- Not with me.
- But in this instance

00:00:20.811 --> 00:00:21.644
we have little bit left over.

00:00:21.644 --> 00:00:24.020
So what we'll do is we
have some sliced pieces,

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.030
they're already cold

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:27.680
and we're gonna put some
into our waffle iron.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.840
- Oh, so you like, you chill it.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:30.673
- You chill it.

00:00:30.673 --> 00:00:31.640
So this is like, when
you have it leftover,

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:33.831
you take it out the casserole dish.

00:00:33.831 --> 00:00:34.664
- Oh God.

00:00:34.664 --> 00:00:35.920
- So we're gonna add one piece of macaroni

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:37.830
on the bottom.
- Only one's fitting in here.

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.930
- [Millie] Then we're gonna
put some cheese in the middle.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:41.780
- [Drew] Oh, okay, more cheese, sure.

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:44.680
- And then we'll take
another piece of the waffle

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:46.550
and I mean the waffle,
the macaroni and cheese

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:47.410
and we're gonna put it on top.

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:48.740
- Oh another?

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:49.573
Okay, great.
- We're gonna create like

00:00:49.573 --> 00:00:50.406
a little sandwich.

00:00:50.406 --> 00:00:51.270
- Oh.

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:52.890
I mean, yes please.
- And be careful.

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:54.230
That's really hot.

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:55.810
- Yes.
- And then as it melts down

00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:57.920
it'll close some more.
(audience applauds)

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:59.843
And this is what it looks like.

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:03.470
- Oh my God.
- Gooey, nice and cheesy.

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:05.253
And then we have our brisket.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:07.114
So we're just gonna put some on top.

00:01:07.114 --> 00:01:07.947
- Look at this, you guys.

00:01:07.947 --> 00:01:09.130
Look at this.

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:10.030
- I'm gonna put some on top

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:12.733
and you put as little or
as much as you like on top.

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:16.570
Then I have some scallions.

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:17.840
I love a good green onion.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.310
- I love a chive,

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:21.970
a scallion, a shallot, an onion, a garlic.

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:23.265
- Leek.
- A leek!

00:01:23.265 --> 00:01:24.590
(Drew screams excitedly)
- Yes. Ma'am.

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:27.620
- I just made this like leek
based soup the other day.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:30.030
And it was, Oh, it was so good.

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:31.913
- I like all types of onions.

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:34.520
- I'm going big here, Millie

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:36.940
and I can see the onions,
which I really like, they're...

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:38.370
- And you saw how we caramelized them

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:39.660
so they got a little sweeter.

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:41.380
So there is like a good, balanced dish.

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:44.370
And then here I have it with
some, another repurposed dish.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.780
This is my New York Times mango slaw.

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:48.640
And you can use leftover fruit

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:50.070
that you have in your refrigerator.

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:52.890
I have some cabbage,
some carrots in there.

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:55.090
If you have some collard
greens that are leftover,

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:56.530
short 'em up, put them in there.

00:01:56.530 --> 00:02:00.100
This is a wonderful counterbalance
to all of this savory,

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:03.418
cheesy, gooey deliciousness
we have going on.

00:02:03.418 --> 00:02:07.290
(audience applauds)

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:10.038
Well, let's just taste
this, how about we do that?

00:02:10.038 --> 00:02:11.747
- It's just...

00:02:11.747 --> 00:02:13.165
(audience laughs)

00:02:13.165 --> 00:02:13.998
You know what, okay.

00:02:13.998 --> 00:02:14.831
Now...
- You wanna focus on

00:02:14.831 --> 00:02:15.664
